  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-82995\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p></p><p>First, let's rewrite the phrase \"it is pretty or white\" as the equivalent phrase \"it is pretty or it is white.\" The sentence now reads</p><p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The house is pretty, or it is pretty or it is white.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Then, using the associative law, we can move the comma:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The house is pretty or it is pretty, or it is white.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Now, we can simplify the phrase \"the house is pretty or it is pretty\" to just \"the house is pretty.\" The sentence now reads</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The house is pretty, or it is white.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Finally, we can write the sentence more concisely as</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The house is pretty or white.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">The house is not pretty or white</div></div>",
